    "summary": "Gown (boubou, tobe); composed of two widths of imported European calico cloth machine-sewn together to form a rectangle. A circular hole has been cut into the centre for the wearer’s head. Gown has four horizontal bands of indigo stitch resist-dyed patterns. The entire cloth has been twice dyed in indigo, once overall, and again after the ties were removed to form a lighter blue decoration within the four decorative bands.",
